      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MiniMax H3 - TURBO 4-step + scene chaining (R9700 / gfx1201)\n\n**Default: 640x352 / 243 frames (10.125 s) - ~3 min.** Low res on purpose: upscale after.\n\n### The one hard rule: STEPS = 4\nThis LoRA is *step-distilled* for the schedule `[1.0, 0.973, 0.9231, 0.8, 0.0]`.\nThat single huge `0.8 -> 0.0` jump is the whole trick. **8 steps looks WORSE** -\nit inserts a `0.6316` point the LoRA has never seen. Do not raise it.\nThe **Turbo Sampler** is also required; a plain `KSamplerSelect` will not work.\n\n### Artifacting dial\n`MiniMaxH3TurboLoRA -> strength`: `1.00` sharpest/grainiest, `0.85` cleaner,\n**`0.70` <- set here**, cleanest. Below the author's 0.8-1.2 range, so go back up\nif it ever looks soft. This LoRA is over-sharp by design, so *lower* strength\nfixes crunch - a sharpen filter makes it worse.\n\n### Token budget - this governs SPEED, not resolution alone\nCost is driven by `latent_t x (W/32) x (H/32)`. Measured knee on this card:\n**<= ~17k tokens is fast (~14-17 s/it); ~21k is already 5x slower (~76 s/it)**\nbecause 20 GB of weights leaves only ~5.5 GB for activations.\n\n| canvas @ 243f (10.1 s) | tokens | speed |\n|---|---|---|\n| **640x352** | **15,840** | **fast <- default** |\n| 640x384 | 17,280 | fast-ish |\n| 704x384 | 19,008 | near knee |\n| 864x480 | 29,160 | slow, avoid |\n\nAt 124 frames (5.2 s) instead, 864x480 = 14,985 tokens and is fast.\n**Trade duration against resolution - you cannot have both.**\n\n### Scene chaining (character continuity)\nThe two `LoadImage` nodes are **muted** by default. To continue a scene:\n\n1. Render clip A.\n2. `python extract_last_frame.py H3_turbo_chain_00001_.mp4`\n   (writes into ComfyUI's `input` folder - LoadImage cannot read `output`)\n3. Select the **first_frame** node, press **Ctrl+M** to un-mute, pick the PNG.\n4. Change the prompt to clip B's action. Render.\n\nClip B then starts from clip A's literal final pixels. This is what the `fl2va`\ncheckpoint is for, and it beats any prompt wording for consistency.\n\nAlso keep a **verbatim character block** in every prompt - same words, every\ntime. Paraphrasing is how designs drift.\n\n> Chaining changes the sequence length, so the first chained render at a given\n> size pays a one-time ~3 min attention autotune. Cached after that.\n\n### Launch\n`Launch ComfyUI AMD RDNA4.bat` - sets `--disable-smart-memory` and the Inductor\ncache the autotuned attention kernel needs.\n"
      ]
    },
